    limitingContext: "Law enforcement can respond to a bomb, assault, or other genuine public-safety emergency at a polling site. Federal law sharply restricts placing troops or armed men where a general or special election is held, and other federal and state laws prohibit intimidation. The administration’s February assurance is important counterevidence; Bannon’s demand is advocacy by a private ally, not state policy.",
