    status: "Final judgment vacates policy; defendants waived appeal; future lawful policymaking preserved",
    publicationState: "Published",
    factualSummary: "An October 14 final judgment vacates USCIS Policy Alert PA-2025-21 and reinstates the relevant 2017 policy. The displaced policy restricted nongovernmental groups from helping new citizens register to vote at administrative naturalization ceremonies. Following the parties' joint stipulation, the court adopted its earlier findings on specified claims and resolved the merits for plaintiffs; remaining claims were dismissed without prejudice. The League announced the outcome October 15, and Democracy Docket reported the restored access. The filed judgment controls the event date.",
